2026-08-18T15:31:25.4535544Z > 
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4536246Z > # Phase 18 is the package's exhaustive simulation/reporting harness, and the
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4537300Z > # structured-conversion contract is a generated 22,000-assertion audit. Keep
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4538321Z > # both in repository CI, but do not rerun them during routine CRAN checks.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4538932Z > #
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4539602Z > # The second group is a CRAN check-time budget. Measured on 2026-08-10 (receipts
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4540357Z > # in docs/dev-log/release/0.7.0-cran-gate/test-timings.csv): the CRAN lane ran
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4540929Z > # 1160 s locally and 29-30 min of `checking tests` on win-builder, far above
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4541471Z > # CRAN's ~10-minute incoming guidance. Seventeen files carried 747 s of that
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4542043Z > # 1160 s; excluding them leaves 413 s locally (~6.9 min), projecting to ~10 min
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4542728Z > # on Windows at the measured 1.50x local->win-builder factor.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4543052Z > #
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4543463Z > # These are statistical-validation suites -- bivariate association sandwiches,
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4544075Z > # the G4/G5 missing-response foundation, zero-one-beta, bivariate Gaussian, and
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4544679Z > # the profile-target matrix -- not "does the package install and work" tests.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4545588Z > # They still run in full in repository CI, where NOT_CRAN=true. Nothing is
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4546213Z > # deleted and no test is weakened; this only changes which lane runs them.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4546593Z > #
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4546971Z > # The patterns are ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored "zero-one-beta" also
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4547526Z > # matches test-missing-predictor-zero-one-beta.R, and an unanchored
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4548126Z > # "biv-gaussian" also matches test-missing-response-biv-gaussian.R -- neither is
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4548662Z > # intended, and both must keep running on the CRAN lane.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4548965Z > #
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4549369Z > # `^julia` excludes every test-julia-*.R file. That alone is NOT enough: CRAN-lane
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4549963Z > # files such as test-binomial-response.R still call engine = "julia" inside
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4550548Z > # expect_error(), and Workflow G now admits fixed-effect binomial into the Julia
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4551149Z > # bridge, so the call reaches JuliaCall::julia_setup() before any rejection.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4551708Z > # Ligges win-builder (2026-08-16/17) hung there for ~10448s even after #1061.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4552450Z > # Defense in depth: (1) this filter, (2) drm_skip_live_julia() in live tests,
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4553022Z > # (3) drm_julia_setup() hard-blocks the CRAN lane unless DRMTMB_JULIA_TESTS=true.
2026-08-18T15:31:25.4553487Z > # The full suite still runs when NOT_CRAN=true.
